Holdings and changed its name to Palomar Holdings, Inc. The company was incorporated in 2013 and is headquartered in La Jolla, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. D. McDonald Armstrong | Founder, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Compensation: $5.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 439 people. Revenue per employee of $2.0M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 41%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $932K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Palomar Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.2B market cap on $876M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +39% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $409M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 47 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6866329361841006},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (96% sell ratio, net $12.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 20% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Earnings Strength Altering The Investment Case For Palomar Holdings Stock (PLMR)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-plmr/palomar-holdings/news/earnings-strength-altering-the-investment-case-for-palomar-h","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794569606.025,"o